cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Lambert 1912: a dataset of the colonial elite of Tunisia
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, please cite both this repository and the source
  volume it was built from.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Hammami
    given-names: Mohamed Dhia
    email: mhammami@syr.edu
repository-code: https://github.com/MedDhia/Lambert1912ElitesTN
abstract: >-
  Machine-readable tables built from Paul Lambert's Dictionnaire illustre de la
  Tunisie: choses et gens de Tunisie (Tunis, 1912), an illustrated who's-who and
  gazetteer of the French Protectorate. Covers 1,307 biographical notices, 736
  localities and 159 associations, with individual attributes, career sequences,
  French and beylical honours, and the affiliation ties linking people to
  associations, public bodies and places. Built from the BnF/Gallica ALTO OCR of
  ark:/12148/bpt6k5505300s.
keywords:
  - Tunisia
  - French Protectorate
  - colonial elites
  - prosopography
  - social network analysis
  - historical text mining
license: MIT
references:
  - type: book
    title: >-
      Dictionnaire illustre de la Tunisie: choses et gens de Tunisie
    authors:
      - family-names: Lambert
        given-names: Paul
    year: 1912
    publisher:
      name: C. Saliba aine
    location:
      name: Tunis
    url: https://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k5505300s
    notes: Digitised by the Bibliotheque nationale de France.
